WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.489
Endpoint Detection and Response is a security capability that monitors endpoint activity,

00:00:04.489 --> 00:00:06.317
detects suspicious behavior, supports investigation,

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:08.877
and helps responders contain or remediate threats.

00:00:08.877 --> 00:00:12.534
The detection part helps teams notice unusual or risky activity.

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:16.557
The response part helps teams act before an incident spreads further.

00:00:16.557 --> 00:00:21.311
EDR tools typically collect telemetry from endpoints, such as process execution, file activity,

00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:24.237
network connections, registry changes, login activity, script execution,

00:00:24.237 --> 00:00:25.700
and suspicious command-line behavior.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:31.186
This telemetry gives analysts a more detailed view than a simple allowed or blocked message.

00:00:31.186 --> 00:00:34.477
The goal is not only to block known malware.

00:00:34.477 --> 00:00:39.597
The goal is to help security teams understand what happened, how far it spread,

00:00:39.597 --> 00:00:42.157
and what action should be taken next.

00:00:42.157 --> 00:00:46.546
EDR is especially useful when an event is not obviously good or

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.740
bad and the analyst needs context.
